  "security_implications": "The cfg_block signal is a configuration lock that gates writes to HMAC configuration registers. If external logic writes to configuration while cfg_block is asserted, an attacker could alter keys, modes, or digest targets mid-operation, potentially leading to secret leakage, faulty digests, or integrity failures. The priority override of hash_start_or_continue over reg_hash_stop/reg_hash_done could cause the lock to remain asserted longer than expected under simultaneous toggle, increasing the window of vulnerability.",
